  "cleanup": "Temporary acceptance Jobs, ConfigMaps and egress policies removed after verified retrieval; model port-forward closed. Existing worker/Secrets/ServiceAccounts unchanged.",
  "rulings": [
    "Ruling: create a managed isolated worktree under implementation authorization \u2014 prevents changing the original checkout \u2014 cost if wrong: changes are on a separate feature branch to integrate.",
    "Ruling: initial operational bounds/resources remain the approved builder defaults, not a GPU requirement \u2014 CPU audition proves feasibility \u2014 cost if wrong: acceptance may require resizing before rollout.",
    "Task 2: Ruling: keep revision-2 rendering accepted alongside latest revision 3 \u2014 preserving silent rendering is required by spec \u2014 cost if wrong: extra compatibility path must stay tested.",
    "Task 3: Ruling: validate source-backed examples and actual configured-model behavior rather than grep new prose \u2014 exact-text assertions would mirror guidance, contrary to writing-good-tests \u2014 cost if wrong: semantic behavior remains a measured model acceptance check, not deterministic CI proof.",
    "Task 3: Ruling: configured model is cluster-internal; use a local port-forward and existing worker model credentials in memory for bounded same-model API acceptance \u2014 no new provider or persisted secret \u2014 cost if wrong: CLI-specific behavior is separately retained as operational validation. OpenCode CLI emitted no completion within the bounded smoke; direct same-model baseline succeeded.",
    "Task 3: Ruling: use CI-pinned Ruff 0.15.11, not newly installed 0.17.4 \u2014 newer rules flagged 69 unrelated existing findings \u2014 cost if wrong: newer lint migration remains separate work. Pinned full lint passes.",
    "Task 4: Ruling: round measured scene intervals upward to the next 30fps frame and retain exact frame counts \u2014 avoids cumulative fractional-frame drift and never truncates speech \u2014 cost if wrong: at most 1/30s extra pause per scene. Spec clarified accordingly.",
    "Task 4: Ruling: generate the separate renderer hash lock with uv pip compile instead of pip-tools \u2014 pip-tools spent minutes and gigabytes rediscovering distribution metadata/hashes, while uv resolved the working audited set promptly \u2014 cost if wrong: requires the already-used uv tool for renderer-lock regeneration. Root dependency declarations/lock workflow remain unchanged; renderer install is fully hash-checked.",
    "Task 4: Ruling: upgrade renderer CPU Torch from audition 2.8.0 to 2.15.0 \u2014 normal pip-audit skipped local +cpu versions, so audited normalized versions; 2.8.0 had nine reported advisories, 2.15.0 has none \u2014 cost if wrong: validate Kokoro compatibility/performance again offline. English model is a direct upstream hash-verified wheel outside PyPI advisory coverage; retain that explicit audit limitation.",
    "Task 4: Ruling: replace the unavailable/mismatching John Van Sickle archive with public digest-pinned mwader/static-ffmpeg 7.0.2, retaining GPL/source/version notices and exact executable hash checks \u2014 the fixed URL also returned HTML and private historical image cannot be pulled anonymously by CI \u2014 cost if wrong: validate codec/timing parity with this different static build before acceptance. No checksum bypass or blind hash update.",
    "Task 5: Ruling: correct schema-2 graph edges to actual TopoLoop string pairs in both validators \u2014 real graph acceptance exposed Task 2 incorrectly requiring objects \u2014 cost if wrong: browser graph validation remains the final check. Added shared real graph fixture and watched Python/Node fail then pass.",
    "Task 5: Ruling: copy renderer runtime sources after dependency/model layers and include new helper in image \u2014 necessary packaging and avoids repeated dependency/model downloads on renderer edits \u2014 cost if wrong: image build validates all copies.",
    "Task 6: Ruling: concatenate padded PCM and encode AAC only once, rather than AAC per scene \u2014 avoids per-segment encoder priming and drift while satisfying measured scene intervals \u2014 cost if wrong: actual tone/cut/full-decode acceptance checks synchronization.",
    "Task 6: Ruling: propagate subprocess nonzero/timeout errors from the existing process-group helper, while wrapper preserves valid partial output \u2014 otherwise a failed speech process could enter record \u2014 cost if wrong: legacy timeout internal test now expects the error while still verifies descendants die.",
    "Task 7: Ruling: add a small shared policy module and wire narration opt-in through worker Job/CronJob/launcher \u2014 the plan's listed files omitted the actual environment forwarding path \u2014 cost if wrong: YAML behavior test and launcher syntax check cover wiring; no live configuration is changed.",
    "Task 7: Ruling: image capability remains a tested-operator precondition, not inferred from digest text \u2014 no registry capability metadata contract exists \u2014 cost if wrong: incompatible images fail explicit format/asset checks rather than producing narrated success; rollout requires actual pinned-image acceptance.",
    "Task 8: Ruling: crop browser captures using probed recorded-media duration, not context wall-clock preroll \u2014 constrained real render produced a 5.733s scene for a 6s timeline because Playwright's first frame arrived late; the 6.96s raw capture contained enough footage \u2014 cost if wrong: capture tail shifts illustrative animation by roughly 0.15s; measured scene/audio boundaries stay exact. Added delayed-capture FFmpeg RED\u2192GREEN regression; retain <=0.25s gate.",
    "Task 8: Ruling: remove redundant recursive image-wide chmod \u2014 image history showed a 2.94GB copy-up layer; dependencies are already world-readable and asset preparer explicitly sets 0644 \u2014 cost if wrong: constrained arbitrary-UID acceptance catches unreadable assets. This reduces delivery size without relaxing runtime isolation.",
    "Task 8: Ruling: use selected source excerpts for configured-model semantic acceptance \u2014 whole report/log context produced self-contradictory false positives despite matching facts; compact exact selected excerpts received substantive review \u2014 cost if wrong: code still resolves selectors against the complete hashed bundle; no approval is fabricated. Real reviews corrected classifications and an implied cross-platform claim first.",
    "Task 8: Ruling: retain human listening as an explicit rollout gate \u2014 this environment can verify exact scripts, PCM, audio timing and full decoding but does not provide a trustworthy human listening judgment \u2014 cost if wrong: pronunciation defects must be caught using the delivered videos/audio before live activation; do not claim listened acceptance.",
    "Task 8: Ruling: enforce exact segment/final frame counts and pad at most0.1s of terminal video before trimming to reviewed frame count \u2014 real Omnigent capture lost5/4781 frames through 25fps\u219230fps rounding; within0.25s but cumulative longer decks could fail \u2014 cost if wrong: final held visual frame may repeat up to0.1s; audio timing/text stay unchanged. A genuine retained WebM reproduces181expected/180actual RED\u2192GREEN; fabricated CFR fixture did not reproduce, so did not count it as proof. Rebuilding/re-running all full cases on acceptance2 image before final claims.",
    "Final review scheduling Ruling: perform the one fresh whole-branch code review while final pinned-image runtime acceptance finishes \u2014 source behavior is frozen and independent of minutes-long media capture; only acceptance records/docs follow unless the reviewer finds a defect \u2014 cost if wrong: any resulting code fix needs regression tests and affected runtime revalidation before final completion. No extra implementer or per-task reviewer is dispatched.",
    "Final: Ruling: live Drive publication is blocked by invalid_grant \u2014 retain tested journal/recovery implementation and explicitly withhold publication success \u2014 cost if wrong: real upload/reconcile must be tested after credential repair before rollout.",
    "Final: Ruling: human listening/pronunciation remains a rollout gate \u2014 exact script/PCM/timing/decoding are machine-verified, no trustworthy human listening claim is available here \u2014 cost if wrong: listen to delivered full narration before activation.",
    "Final: Ruling: concurrent final long/OCP acceptance must finish before final claims \u2014 collect exact image/input/output metrics and rerun affected paths after fixes \u2014 cost if wrong: an unfinished run cannot establish readiness and remains visibly pending.",
    "Final: Ruling: arbitrary image digest compatibility is not inferred \u2014 use tested capability/model identity as the operator precondition \u2014 cost if wrong: incompatible images fail closed; upgrade worker/renderer together only after pinned-image acceptance.",
    "Task 8: Ruling: remove the acceptance harness's forced hostUsers=false after container runtime setgroups failure \u2014 the standard tokenless profile runs under required restricted-v2 with assigned nonroot UID \u2014 cost if wrong: user-namespace-specific clusters need their own acceptance; no live security policy was weakened."
